; W2 dep spec for `--wrapper-requests` stub-fidelity + residual-mismatch hard errors.
; `coin = uint` is a transparent primitive alias, so a `[* coin]` request is DIRECTLY WASM-EXPOSABLE
; (`Vec<Coin>`, no wrapper class) — the dep-side intake must diagnose it as an unfaithful consumer
; stub rather than a name<->shape disagreement. `credential`/`nal` (`@no_alias`) exercise the residual
; name<->shape mismatch's element-resolution appendix: a `[* nal]` request derives `CredentialList`,
; not the listed `NalList`, because `@no_alias` transparently substitutes `nal` to `credential`.
coin = uint
credential = [n: uint]
nal = credential ; @no_alias
root = [c: coin, cr: credential, n: nal]
